  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mi>Co</mi><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><msub><mo>)</mo><mn>5</mn></msub><mi>Cl</mi></mrow></mfenced><msub><mi>Cl</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math></p><p>The primary valency is the ionisable valency.&nbsp; Oxidation number of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Co</mi></math>&nbsp;is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></math>. So, primary valency is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math>. Secondary valency refers&nbsp;the coordination number. It is an octahedral complex so, secondary valency is 6.</p>",
